*Heading
abq2ccx example: *MPC PIN / TIE / LINK on nodes with a *TRANSFORM (validate_with_ccx.py
compares it with the same model without the transforms). Two orthotropic blocks: A is
clamped at x = 0; B is pinned (PIN, TIE) to A at x = 1, where B's face has a cylindrical
and A's face a rectangular *TRANSFORM; B's far face is pinned to the reference point RP
(loaded); a LINK holds B's node 135 at its distance from a clamped anchor; node 135 has a
rectangular *TRANSFORM. Abaqus' PIN, TIE and LINK constrain the global displacements, so
the transforms change nothing in Abaqus.
